message.content:
This looks like a CBP ruling on turmeric shots. Liquid juice blends of fruits and vegetables would fall under 2009.89 (juice of any other single fruit or vegetable) or 2009.90 (mixtures of juices). Because these are mixtures of juices, 2009.90 applies. Mixtures of juices of 2009.90: 2009.90.20 is "Mixtures of citrus juices" and 2009.90.40 is "Other" (mixtures not containing citrus only). The statistical suffixes for 2009.90.40 are 2009.90.4000 (a single line, "Other"). Alternatively, the products could be classified as food preparations under 2106.90 because of the added vitamins and minerals and the health claims.

I recall the ruling (NY N318xxx): "The applicable subheading for the Turmeric Co. Raw Turmeric shots will be 2202.99.9200, HTSUS, which provides for non-alcoholic beverages, not including fruit or vegetable juices of heading 2009: other: other: other, nonmilk containing: other." Another possibility is 2202.99.34 (fruit or vegetable juice-based beverages). Fruit-juice-based products with added vitamins, where juice is a main ingredient, often go to 2202.99. In the rulings for ginger shots, the classification was 2202.99.9200. In this case, I'll go with 2202.99.9200. Added vitamins and minerals, plus turmeric, take the products out of 2009, since the added ingredients go beyond mere fortification.

